MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Corazon feels like a natural next choice because Santana's expressive guitar playing connects with what draws me to Clapton and Hendrix; it is the one album I would choose today.",
    "The later Beatles songs fit my interest in classic rock songwriting, while Norah Jones offers a piano-led direction that appeals after You Should Be So Lucky."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "A broad 80s compilation and Patsy Cline's traditional country do not connect closely enough with the blues and roots rock I want right now.",
    "Greatest Hits and Definitive Collection leave me unsure whose music I would get, so I cannot connect them to my interests. Lb - Kill The Lights also gives me no clear reason to expect the sound I want."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to assume that familiar older music will appeal to me regardless of its sound, but an older recording alone is not enough.",
    "Hit collections seem to be treated as natural choices for me, although I care more about the particular performer and songs than whether an album collects hits."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The expressive guitar playing and blues-rooted feel connecting several of my recent albums matter more to me than a broad connection to rock or familiar music.",
    "An album can fit my taste without being something I want to choose now. I would consider the Beatles, Norah Jones, and possibly Wallflower another time, but Corazon has the strongest pull today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly capture my interest in classic songwriting and expressive musicianship, but stretch that interest too far toward general nostalgia and hit collections."
}
